{{Quote|Need an extra hand? I got four!|Four Arms.<ref>''[[Super Alien Hero Buddy Adventures (Episode)|Super Alien Hero Buddy Adventures]]''</ref>}}
Whenever [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] needs to smash, throw or beat up something, Four Arms is the alien of choice. This formidable four-armed alien can use his tremendous strength to dish out the punishment. Four Arms was able to go toe-to-toe with, swing around and throw a [[Living Mammoth|reanimated mammoth]];<ref name="WBC">''[[Washington B.C.]]''</ref> damage the [[Great One]]'s shell;<ref name="TBT">''[[The Big Tick]]''</ref> easily lift and swing around a massive pillar; rival [[Ah Puch]] in strength;<ref name="UW">''[[Ultimate Weapon]]''</ref> knock out Clancy and destroy a small Rock Monster in a single punch;<ref name="N10P2">''[[Ben 10 vs. Negative 10: Part 2]]''</ref> effortlessly launch [[Azmuth (Classic)|Azmuth]]'s [[Azmuth's Father|father]] in [[Mechamorph Armor|Mechamorph armor]] over the horizon;<ref name="DAA">'''''[[Ben 10: Destroy All Aliens]]'''''</ref> tackle [[Malware]] through several [[Galvan (Classic)|Galvan]] houses;<ref name="TH">''[[Trouble Helix]]''</ref> throw [[Rex Salazar (Generator Rex)|Rex]] hard enough to shatter his [https://generatorrex.fandom.com/wiki/Rex_Salazar%27s_machines#Smack_hands Smack Hands] and knock back [[Alpha]];<ref name="HU">''[[Ben 10-Generator Rex: Heroes United|Ben 10/Generator Rex: Heroes United]]''</ref> overpower [[Looma Red Wind]], the princess of the Red Wind Kingdom, despite female Tetramands being generally stronger than their male counterparts<ref>[[Rook Blonko]]</ref><ref name="MHR">''[[Many Happy Returns]]''</ref> and harm and knock around [[Exo-Skull]].<ref name="LDTWA">''[[Let's Do the Time War Again]]''</ref> The older Four Arms grows, the stronger he becomes.<ref>''[[The Forge of Creation]]''</ref> Technically speaking, Four Arms is physically stronger than [[Methanosian]]s and [[Vaxasaurian (Classic)|Vaxasaurians]] at base size.{{Refn|[[:File:Kevin's Previous Girlfriends.PNG]]|group = DM}}

Four Arms' sheer strength allows him to create devastating shock waves, by either simply punching something<ref name="MHR" /> or slamming his fists on the ground.<ref name="TA">''[[The Alliance]]''</ref><ref name="N10P2" /><ref name="MHR" /> Additionally, Four Arms can create shock waves by clapping all four of his hands together,<ref name="GO">''[[Game Over]]''</ref><ref name="MW" /><ref name="HU" /> a move nicknamed the "Big Smack".{{Refn|''[[Ben 10 Ultimate Alien: The Complete Guide]]'', [[:File:UA TCG Pg 28.png|Page 28]]|group = guide}} Ben learned this ability from [[Tini]].{{Refn|[[:File:Four Arms Sonic Clap.png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref name="GO" />{{Refn|[[:File:Tini taught Ben.png]]|group = pop-up}}{{Refn|''Azmuth & Galactic Enforcers Ben''|group = DVD}} Furthermore, by punching the ground, Four Arms can cause pillars of rock to erupt.<ref name="MW">''[[Monster Weather]]''</ref><ref name="N10P2" /><ref name="ROE">''[[Rules of Engagement]]''</ref>

Four Arms has a high level of durability due to his tough and thorny skin,{{Refn|[[:File:Four Arms Thick Skin.png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref name="GO" /> being able to survive a fall from hundreds of feet in the air that left behind a massive crater;<ref name="WBC" /> endure a large energy blast from the Great One;<ref name="TBT" /> take multiple blows from Ah Puch;<ref name="UW" /> survive an energy blast point-blank from a large [[Mechadroid]] <ref name="TV">''[[The Visitor]]''</ref> and withstand several strikes from other Tetramands, such as Looma Red Wind<ref name="MHR" /><ref name="Cat">''[[Catfight]]''</ref> and [[Kolar]], the latter of whom was able to overpower and defeat Four Arms.<ref name="BT">''[[Basic Training]]''</ref> In correlation to his durable skin, Four Arms is highly resistant to fire and intense heat, such as that generated by a [[Pyronite (Classic)|Pyronite]].<ref>''[[Framed]]''</ref>

Four Arms can jump several times his own height, at least seven stories up, in a single bound.<ref name="WBC" /><ref name="TA" /><ref name="BaDGtMS" />

Four Arms has enhanced reflexes, as he was able to catch and redirect missiles<ref name="DAA" /> in a single motion.<ref name="TGE" />

Four Arms is immune to extremely cold temperatures, demonstrated when he fought [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]]'s [[Yeti (Classic)|yeti]] on top of a snowy mountain,<ref name="EfA">''[[Escape From Aggregor]]''</ref> and when he was able to survive on [[Mikd'lty]].<ref name="MoI">''[[Map of Infinity (Episode)|Map of Infinity]]''</ref>

Four Arms is also resistant to strong winds, such as those generated by a [[Geochelone Aerios]], as shown with [[Looma Red Wind|Looma]].<ref name="Cat" />

Four Arms can climb up walls by pushing his fingers into them.<ref name="GhO">''[[Ghostfreaked Out]]''</ref>

Four Arms' great strength even extends to his jaws, allowing him to bite down on dense metal.<ref>''[[The Unnaturals]]''</ref>

==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow">
MS (5).png|Constrained by Large Size
K10 (399).png|Electricity Vulnerability
Rumble (436).png|Sedative Quill Vulnerability
Side (753).png|Affected by Cold Virus
</gallery>
Four Arms' bulk can sometimes become a disadvantage, as his immense size makes him an easy target for enemy attacks. Four Arms' size can make moving through areas designed for small species, like the [[Rustbucket (Classic)|Rustbucket 1]]<ref name="K11"/> and [[Rustbucket II|2]],<ref>''[[Moonstruck]]''</ref> difficult.

Four Arms can feel tremendous pain from electricity,<ref name="TGE" /> such as that generated by [[Galvanic Mechamorph (Classic)|Galvanic Mechamorphs]]<ref name="Ken 10">''[[Ken 10]]''</ref> and [[Gimlinopithecus]].<ref name="HU" /><ref name="MHR" />

Four Arms can become drowsy from sedative quills.<ref>''[[Ready to Rumble]]''</ref>

Four Arms can be infected with the cold virus, causing his strength and stamina to be severely reduced.<ref>''[[Side Effects]]''</ref>

